<.shell title="Typography" current={:typography}>
  <h1>Typography</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    IBM Plex Sans, six sizes, three weights. Every size has a fixed line height on the 4px grid.
  </p>

  <h2>Type scale</h2>
  <p>
    These six are the only sizes. Each is a token pair: <code>--fs-md</code>
    and <code>--lh-md</code>.
  </p>
  <.table id="type-scale" rows={type_scale()}>
    <:col :let={{name, _size, _line, _use}} label="Token" class="w-px mono">{name}</:col>
    <:col :let={{_name, size, _line, _use}} label="Size" class="w-px" align="right">
      {size}px
    </:col>
    <:col :let={{_name, _size, line, _use}} label="Line" class="w-px" align="right">
      {line}px
    </:col>
    <:col :let={{_name, _size, _line, use}} label="Use">{use}</:col>
    <:col :let={{_name, size, line, _use}} label="Sample" class="whitespace-nowrap">
      <span style={"font-size: #{size}px; line-height: #{line}px"}>Missing hiker</span>
    </:col>
  </.table>

  <h2>Weights</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <p class="paragraph">
      <span class="font-normal">400 Regular</span>: body text, table cells, hints.
    </p>
    <p class="paragraph">
      <span class="font-semibold">600 Semibold</span>: labels, buttons, table headers, tags.
    </p>
    <p class="paragraph"><span class="font-bold">700 Bold</span>: headings, errors, emphasis.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Headings</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <h1 class="title">Activities, 2025</h1>
    <h2 class="heading">Attendance</h2>
    <h3 class="subheading">Recommended changes</h3>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    <code>.title</code>
    on the h1, 2xl. <code>.heading</code>
    on an h2, xl. <code>.subheading</code>
    on an h3, lg. One h1 per page. Space above a heading is bigger than below, so it belongs to what follows.
  </p>

  <h2>Body text</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <p class="lead">Lead text introduces a page in one or two sentences.</p>
    <p class="paragraph max-w-prose">
      Body text at 16px. Search and rescue managers read this between calls, so it stays short and
      plain. Lines stop at about 70 characters, which keeps long paragraphs readable on a wide
      screen.
    </p>
    <p class="paragraph text-sm">
      Small text, 14px, for secondary detail under a table or a form.
    </p>
    <p class="hint">A hint, 14px and muted, under a label.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    <code>.lead</code>, <code>.paragraph</code>, <code>text-sm</code>, and <code>.hint</code>, which is also the class for any small, muted line. Muted text at body size is <code>text-text-muted</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Numbers</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <p class="paragraph">
      Figures are tabular everywhere, so columns of hours line up without extra work:
    </p>
    <p class="paragraph text-right w-fit">
      212h 30m<br />18h 5m<br />1,204 hours
    </p>
    <p class="paragraph">
      Codes and IDs use the mono face: <span class="mono">TCL-2025-014</span>, activity <span class="mono">2025-0412</span>. Dates do not: Sep 28, 2025.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Code, captions, and small print</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <pre class="code-block">claude mcp add --transport http sarduty https://sarduty.com/teams/squamish/mcp</pre>
    <div class="caps">Member since</div>
    <p class="paragraph text-lg font-semibold">Sep 2023</p>
    <section class="small-print">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>SAR Duty verifies each card against the team's D4H records.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    <code>.code-block</code>
    on a <code>&lt;pre&gt;</code>
    for a command or a token to copy. <code>.caps</code>, xs semibold capitals, over a value. <code>.small-print</code>, under a rule at the end of a page.
  </p>

  <h2>Links and lists</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <p class="paragraph">
      A <.a href="#">link in a sentence</.a> is underlined and thickens on hover. Link text says
      where it goes: <.a href="#">tax credit letters for 2025</.a>, never "click here".
    </p>
    <ul class="list paragraph">
      <li>Bulleted lists for things in no order.</li>
      <li>Each item is short; full sentences end with a period.</li>
    </ul>
    <ol class="list-decimal list-inside paragraph">
      <li>Numbered lists for steps.</li>
      <li>One action per step.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: <code>&lt;.a&gt;</code> for a link, <code>.list</code> for bullets.
  </p>

  <h2>Arrows</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <p class="paragraph">Ten of your latest activities.</p>
    <p class="action">
      <.a href="#">All your activities</.a>
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>
    An arrow starts a link that stands on its own line as the next thing to do: the Actions in a <a href={
      page_path(:detail_list)
    }>detail list</a>, one link after a section, such as All your activities or Change contact details, or the link at the foot of a card or in an empty state.
  </p>
  <ul class="list">
    <li>Never in a sentence, a table, a menu, the side navigation, or beside a heading.</li>
    <li>
      Never on a link that belongs to a value, such as Open in Google Maps under an address. It sits with the value.
    </li>
    <li>
      A link to the whole list gets one, even under a value, such as All 12 milestones under the latest one.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: <code>&lt;ul class="action-list"&gt;</code>
    for several, <code>&lt;p class="action"&gt;</code>
    for one.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    <code>external=&#123;true&#125;</code>
    for a link that leaves SAR Duty for another service, such as D4H or its help pages: it opens a new tab and ends in an icon that says so.
    The verify site is SAR Duty's own, so its links open in the same tab with no icon.
  </p>
</.shell>
